@page "/components/sidebar"

<PageTitle>Sidebar — Unpoly.Blazor.Shadcn</PageTitle>

<h1 class="doc-h1">Sidebar</h1>
<p class="doc-lede">
    Twenty-three components, and one decision that shapes all of them: where the open state lives.
</p>
<p class="doc-note">
    In a <code>sidebar_state</code> cookie, which is where shadcn keeps it too. The server reads
    it and passes <code>Open</code>, so the first paint is already right — no flash of a sidebar
    opening itself, and no client state to lose in a fragment swap. The trigger and the rail ship
    hidden and reveal themselves: with no JavaScript there is nothing to toggle, and the honest
    fallback is a sidebar that stays open with every link still in it.
</p>
<Example Source="SidebarExample.razor"><SidebarExample /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Reading the cookie</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    One line in the page that renders the layout. Nothing else in the library needs to know.
</p>
<CodeBlock Language="csharp" Title="MainLayout.razor" Class="mt-4 max-w-2xl" Code="@Reading" />

@code {
    const string Reading = """
        @* The cascading HttpContext every Unpoly.Blazor page already has. *@
        <SidebarProvider Open="@(Ctx.Request.Cookies["sidebar_state"] != "false")">
            <Sidebar Collapsible="icon">…</Sidebar>
            <SidebarInset>@Body</SidebarInset>
        </SidebarProvider>
        """;
}
